From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] configs: am335x_evm: drop finduuid from extra env settings

finduuid runs "part uuid mmc 0:2 uuid" to resolve a GPT partition UUID
for root= on the kernel cmdline.  The Optimal Tiny boot contract uses
extlinux.conf for all kernel arguments (root= included), so the U-Boot
env variable is never consumed.  Remove it to reduce unused env surface.

DTB selection is intentionally left to the extlinux.conf fdt directive
instead of the findfdt env; sysboot ignores ${fdtfile} when the config
file carries an explicit fdt line.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [project-specific BeagleBone Optimal boot contract]

--- a/include/configs/am335x_evm.h
+++ b/include/configs/am335x_evm.h
@@ -81,7 +81,6 @@
 #define CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS \
 	DEFAULT_LINUX_BOOT_ENV \
 	"fdtfile=undefined\0" \
-	"finduuid=part uuid mmc 0:2 uuid\0" \
 	"console=ttyO0,115200n8\0" \
 	"partitions=" \
 		"uuid_disk=${uuid_gpt_disk};" \
